                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "ebaee9eb-b423-4ac9-970e-f1b82232cb6a",
                        "entry_id": "f8da1c6e-958a-3ae5-a691-b4bae6d16fd8",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "диффама́циях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0bb15d03-131f-3f00-83a0-55f7a144280f",
                        "entry_id": "f8da1c6e-958a-3ae5-a691-b4bae6d16fd8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн., юр. публичное распространение сведений (часто, но не обязательно ложных), порочащих кого-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb909ade-63cf-4682-bae2-f040cc458edd",
                                "sense_id": "0bb15d03-131f-3f00-83a0-55f7a144280f",
                                "text": "Посвящая всего себя исключительно диффамации и клевете, он далеко не уверен, что занятие это пройдёт ему даром, и всё-таки идёт навстречу побоям."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7cb89510-b438-44af-80ac-a97c29f1b546",
                                "sense_id": "0bb15d03-131f-3f00-83a0-55f7a144280f",
                                "text": "Ежовые рукавицы… Месяц тюрьмы за диффамации… — Всё это у меня уже есть…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "19cf3d7d-1f7e-4b4b-857f-20008868ab10",
                                "sense_id": "0bb15d03-131f-3f00-83a0-55f7a144280f",
                                "text": "Речь шла только о том, имел или не имел по закону издатель право напечатать статью фельетониста и какое он совершил преступление, напечатав её, — диффамацию или клевету, и как диффамация включает в себе клевету или клевета диффамацию, и ещё что-то мало понятное для простых людей о разных статьях и решениях какого-то общего департамента."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "767af6a3-de63-4e55-8d22-ff4efcd23050",
                                "sense_id": "0bb15d03-131f-3f00-83a0-55f7a144280f",
                                "text": "Есть известное правило: «за базар отвечают». В переводе с уличного языка означает, что имела место диффамация. Порча деловой и личной репутации. По умыслу или почему-то там ещё — это уже юридическая сторона проблемы."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "160708bb-2150-4849-9549-b578bf2f1cfc",
                        "source_entry_id": "f8da1c6e-958a-3ae5-a691-b4bae6d16fd8",
                        "source_sense_id": "0bb15d03-131f-3f00-83a0-55f7a144280f",
                        "target_lang_word": "libel",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "libel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f6f7a414-a28c-38c8-bbca-01c03e06ea0b",
                                        "entry_id": "7b54587c-ca28-32fd-ac26-423c1e5a241b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A written or pictorial false statement which unjustly seeks to damage someone's reputation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc7768b6-88c6-407b-a730-6bb84cc42c51",
                                                "sense_id": "f6f7a414-a28c-38c8-bbca-01c03e06ea0b",
                                                "text": "Peter Parker: Spider-Man wasn't trying to attack the city, he was trying to save it. That's slander."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f105a92d-f020-30ec-8170-94b4018aab6b",
                                        "entry_id": "7b54587c-ca28-32fd-ac26-423c1e5a241b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act or tort of displaying such a statement publicly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ff55023f-1ac6-3317-a468-37281a633a3d",
                                        "entry_id": "7b54587c-ca28-32fd-ac26-423c1e5a241b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any defamatory writing; a lampoon; a satire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2f4d314b-a0af-3ecc-82e1-527c06f18214",
                                        "entry_id": "7b54587c-ca28-32fd-ac26-423c1e5a241b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A written declaration or statement by the plaintiff of their cause of action, and of the relief they seek."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d0adf92-0bb5-4465-8531-77940c24a54f",
                                                "sense_id": "2f4d314b-a0af-3ecc-82e1-527c06f18214",
                                                "text": "These provisions of law being in force, the steamer Rio Grande, owned, as was alleged, by persons in Mexico, being in the port of Mobile, in the Southern District of Alabama, certain materialmen, on the 26th of November, 1867, filed separate libels against her in the district court for the said district."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "15743251-64b0-35b7-97b1-8ac0a787e499",
                                        "entry_id": "7b54587c-ca28-32fd-ac26-423c1e5a241b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A brief writing of any kind, especially a declaration, bill, certificate, request, supplication, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8cd76f96-25d9-4958-91f2-b09a4227f36b",
                                                "sense_id": "15743251-64b0-35b7-97b1-8ac0a787e499",
                                                "text": "a libel of forsaking [divorcement]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "libel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "624a2eff-ed6f-3e66-9b56-f02d9f63424b",
                                        "entry_id": "cd0814ed-9247-3543-ad67-86e89b19cf15",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To defame (someone), especially in a manner that meets the legal definition of libel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4b7b59f-4c9b-4e62-95e6-0c26ef18d94b",
                                                "sense_id": "624a2eff-ed6f-3e66-9b56-f02d9f63424b",
                                                "text": "He libelled her when he published that."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d62f6515-274f-4823-9b38-54927b7ec4ec",
                                                "sense_id": "624a2eff-ed6f-3e66-9b56-f02d9f63424b",
                                                "text": "But vvhat ſo pure, vvhich envious tongues vvill ſpare? / Some vvicked vvits have libell'd all the fair."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c004779b-8d09-3ecf-a5da-94e86f48bff6",
                                        "entry_id": "cd0814ed-9247-3543-ad67-86e89b19cf15",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To proceed against (goods, a ship, etc.) by filing a legal claim."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "702f321a-33bb-4db7-9ae5-4782d2403090",
                        "source_entry_id": "f8da1c6e-958a-3ae5-a691-b4bae6d16fd8",
                        "source_sense_id": "0bb15d03-131f-3f00-83a0-55f7a144280f",
                        "target_lang_word": "defamation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "defamation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "394fe247-f616-365e-96bf-2c9b2a29aa00",
                                        "entry_id": "f3835acf-71e6-322a-baeb-25850966d48c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of injuring another person's reputation by any slanderous communication, written or oral; the wrong of maliciously injuring the good name of another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d99e7a4-7a62-470f-a05a-fd7bb51c80d2",
                                                "sense_id": "394fe247-f616-365e-96bf-2c9b2a29aa00",
                                                "text": "She sued his ex-boyfriend for defamation and is seeking $14,000."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d261924-66e3-446f-b888-2b35316a94a9",
                                                "sense_id": "394fe247-f616-365e-96bf-2c9b2a29aa00",
                                                "text": "In a closed trial on December 24, 2004, the People’s Court of Jinshui District in the city of Zhengzhou, Henan Province, convicted Zhang Ruquan, along with his associate Zhang Zhengyao, in a public prosecution on charges of defamation that “seriously undermined social order or the state interest.” The two were sentenced to three years in prison for defaming former Chinese President Jiang Zemin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "142f3666-4acd-4fbf-ac68-55a3edaabe68",
                                                "sense_id": "394fe247-f616-365e-96bf-2c9b2a29aa00",
                                                "text": "An hour later, when the Fox board approved the wire payment for $787.5 million — one of the largest known defamation settlements in history — Fox acknowledged what we needed it to acknowledge: spreading false claims comes with a huge price tag."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d53dc7c-0039-450d-9828-4728e62750f1",
                                                "sense_id": "394fe247-f616-365e-96bf-2c9b2a29aa00",
                                                "text": "Merryday, who was appointed by President Geroge^([sic]) H. W. Bush, said the complaint contains eighty pages of repetitive claims and praise for President Trump, but fails to establish the two counts of defamation alleged."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c77c750e-f2fb-4a1b-9a30-e62e6048e1e0",
                        "source_entry_id": "f8da1c6e-958a-3ae5-a691-b4bae6d16fd8",
                        "source_sense_id": "0bb15d03-131f-3f00-83a0-55f7a144280f",
